    "evidence": "Re-reviewed 2026-08-08. The current Plasma implementation's pause is confined to mint and redeem paths, and its restriction-manager role only administers minter/redeemer roles; no current holder-transfer blacklist, freeze, seizure, or arbitrary holder-burn hook was found. Yuzu's Hypernative/Sentinel documentation describes surgical blocking of malicious wallets from protocol interactions, but does not establish that this control can intercept an ordinary yzUSD ERC-20 transfer. Current reserves also contain issuer-freezable USDT0, syrupUSDT, syrupUSDC, syrupUSDG, USTB, mGLOBAL, USDe, sUSDe, and AUSD; those controls can impair backing or exits but cannot directly freeze a yzUSD holder balance. The prior inherited verdict was invalid because yzUSD has no single resolvable parent identity. Possible is retained honestly because the documented operational-blocking boundary and issuer legal terms could not be proven to exclude holder-token reach.",
